WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.400
Improvisation Studio — An Audience-Directed Laboratory of Human–AI Co-Performance. What happens when a visitor takes the place of an acting teacher?

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.000
01 Set the exercise: A visitor sets an improvisation exercise for two AI performers.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.600
02 The AI sets the scene: A language model generates the given circumstances and each character’s objective.

4
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.600
03 AI · AI: It produces every line live; nothing is pre-scripted.

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.100
DIRECT: Like an acting teacher, the visitor gives a new action to A, B or both.

6
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.600
DIRECT: A role-specific direction is sent only to that character.

7
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:32.000
DIRECT · AI responds: A direction is not a command: the character may follow it, resist it or misread it.

8
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:38.000
TAKE A ROLE: The visitor replaces A or B and types that character’s lines, while the AI partner keeps improvising. The role can be handed back at any time. (Not shown in this recording.)

9
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.500
JOIN: The visitor names a new character and a reason to be there, and a third chair lights up.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.700
JOIN · Human line · C, the Royal Surveyor: C is always human; the system never writes C’s lines.

11
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.300
AI line · A, Aldric: The two AI characters must now deal with a human who has changed the stakes for both of them.

12
00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:02.200
Direct · Take a role · Join. It translates rehearsal-room techniques into a reusable interaction model for human–AI collaboration, in which the human may direct, substitute or co-perform within the same continuous scene. Improvisation Studio · Wei Liu & Feibi Liu · ICHEC 2026 Art Gallery. Prototype demo · Lines illustrative.
